  "prefLabel": "Ec-Wtr 203.18 Rehearing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ec-Wtr 203.18 Rehearing.\n\n(a) A motion for rehearing shall conform to the requirements of RSA 541 and Ec-Wtr 203.09.\n\n(b) Within 10 days of the receipt of a motion for rehearing, the presiding officer shall:\n\n(1) Deny the motion if the presiding officer concludes that:\n\na. The motion was not timely filed; or\n\nb. The motion does not identify any error of fact, reasoning, or law that could change the outcome of the appeal;\n\n(2) Suspend the council’s decision and schedule the motion for consideration by the council at the council’s next scheduled meeting if the presiding officer concludes that ruling on the motion requires consultation with counsel; or\n\n(3) Grant the motion, schedule a rehearing, and suspend the council’s decision pending the outcome of the rehearing.\n\n(c) The presiding officer shall, consistent with Ec-Wtr 203.06, provide notice to the parties of any action taken pursuant to paragraph (b) above.\n\n(d) The scope of a rehearing shall be limited to the issues upon which the motion for rehearing was granted.\n\n(e) After a rehearing, the council shall issue a written decision, consistent with Ec-Wtr 203.17, either affirming, reversing, or modifying its initial decision and stating the reasons therefor.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note # 1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Ec-Wtr 200) #13923, eff 4-11-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ec-wtr200.html"
}
